  way it adds to the dramatic conflict of  the story and the way it takes part in  the world building sounding like it's an  artifact of the world itself  while watching the film to dissect the  score i discovered some cool ways sound  design and mixing are used in the film  like how they got the baron's voice to  just sound so terrifying  so i've decided to make a companion  video to this one that breaks those  elements down you can watch it right now  on nebula nebula is a streaming service  built and owned by creators and the best  way to get nebula and access to that  video is with the curiosity stream  nebula bundle which you can get for less  than 15 a year when you sign up using my  link below on nebula you can see bonus  exclusive content from me like my  breakdown of dude sound design or my  video about omar little's code from the  wire but you'll also get access to all  my usual videos early and without any  ads or sponsors when you sign up for the  bundle using my link you'll also get  access to curiosity stream where you'll  find a ton of educational and  documentary content if you're interested  in seeing very real stunning desert  visuals you could check out the  documentary africa's desert storms on  curiosity stream right now this bundle  is an amazing deal for less than fifteen  15 for an entire year you'll get access  to two streaming services full of  amazing content signing up and watching  on nebula helps support myself and other  independent creators like me click the  link on the screen to sign up now and  watch my video on dunes sound design  [Music]  [Music]


